    "description": "Estimated camera spectral sensitivity, NOT a measurement. Fitted so that the IDT matrices these curves would receive (Academy P-2013-001-style CIE Lab fit, rawtoaces 190-patch training set) reproduce ARRI's 2013 ALEXA native->ACES AP0 matrices at 17 CCTs, under a 4-component PCA prior built from the 52 Apache-2.0 curves in rawtoaces-data. Each channel normalised to peak 1; relative channel gains are not identifiable from white-balanced matrices and are not needed for white-balanced emulation. The curves are moved by a hue push of 4.5 degrees (beyond_matrix_limit, owner decision 2026-10-26: \"4.5°\"): the curve that renders orange, red and ochre reflectances 4.5 degrees of CIELAB hue toward yellow, with matrix RMS 0.0241 per coefficient, past the 24-variant ensemble (0.0064 to 0.0093; without the push 0.0067), so it agrees with ARRI's matrices less well than the ensemble does. It is a choice, not a fit that ARRI's matrices ask for. See README for accuracy and caveats.",
